# Text is stored with LF in the repository (it already is, every file) and checked out with LF
# on every platform, whatever core.autocrlf says on the machine. Before this, autocrlf wrote
# CRLF on checkout while editors, clang-format and generators wrote LF, so the working tree
# mixed both per file and every touched file warned about being converted.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries: never converted, never diffed as text. Detection would catch most of these on its
# own; naming them means a file that happens to look like text cannot be mangled.
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.ktx2   binary
*.glb    binary
*.blend  binary
*.ttf    binary
*.otf    binary
*.wav    binary
*.ogg    binary
*.dll    binary
*.so     binary
*.so.*   binary
*.lib    binary
*.a      binary
*.exe    binary
*.pdb    binary
